6: /// <summary>
7: /// FR-MCP-040 ac-1 (BDPv4 mock gate, PR 87 slice P): the server reads a requirement's stored CreatedAtUtc and
8: /// UpdatedAtUtc text into the value it sends, keeping the stored offset, and reads a blank or unreadable stored value as
9: /// null; a mapping reports the earliest stored creation time of its links. A stored value without a complete date (its
10: /// year, month and day stated in the text) reads as null and is ignored for a mapping, so no part of a reported value
11: /// comes from the read clock or a parser default. Fixed rows and an independent scripted reader; wrong readers (read
12: /// time, always null, offset converted, latest link instead of earliest, a fixed local offset, a date filled from the
13: /// clock, the year found in the text) are rejected by the same assertions inside this passing harness. No store or
14: /// environment is read; the scripted reader reads no clock.
15: /// </summary>
16: /// <remarks>
17: /// <list type="table">
18: /// <listheader><term>Date</term><description>Requirements; AC; change and reason</description></listheader>
19: /// <item><term>2026-11-02</term><description>FR-MCP-040 ac-1: added the stored-time reader contract (mock gate ug-r9-mockgate-p-1).</description></item>
20: /// <item><term>2026-11-02</term><description>FR-MCP-040 ac-1 (appended "A stored time written without an offset is read as UTC"): added the offset-less row and a wrong reader that applies a fixed local offset, because no row pinned that case (operator 2026-11-02: "UTC").</description></item>
21: /// <item><term>2026-11-02</term><description>FR-MCP-040 ac-1 (appended "A read never fills a missing date from the clock"): added rows for a time alone, a date without a year, a date alone and a complete date in another order, a mapping row with an incomplete link time, and the wrong reader "date filled from the clock" (the earlier production parse), because hostile validation finding R9-F4 showed a time alone took the read day's date (operator 2026-11-02: "Strengthen 5 ACs, fix all 8 (Recommended)").</description></item>
22: /// <item><term>2026-11-03</term><description>FR-MCP-040 ac-1 (appended "A readable stored time states its year, its month and its day as date components"): added rows for a year and month alone (numeric and in words), year digits only in a fraction and a complete date with the month in words, two mapping rows (an incomplete earlier-looking link, every link incomplete), and the wrong reader "year in the text" (the round 9 production reader), because hostile validation round 10 finding R10-F1 showed a year and month alone passed with day 1 (operator 2026-11-03: "don't gate on me between rounds").</description></item>
23: /// </list>
